{
  "name": "NamedTypeIsRegistered",
  "comment": "Stage 1 (decision 867): a type named in a step is the registered one — its kind knows\nits mime AND its extension. For `as text/md`, the registered md kind is text's\n`[Format(\"md\", \"text/markdown\", \".md\", \".markdown\")]`: mime \"text/markdown\", extensions\n[\".md\", \".markdown\"]. Red on runtime2: today `type.@this(...)` at `type/this.cs:149`\nmakes a fresh `kind.@this(\"md\")` from the name — a bare kind whose `_mime` and\n`_extension` default to `[]`, so both `%x!type.kind.mime[0]%` and\n`%x!type.kind.extension[0]%` read null.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "set %x% = \"a\" as text/md",
      "line": {
        "number": 9
      },
      "code": [
